---
/** What this site does with a visitor's data. Keep it true: update it when the site changes. */
import Base from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="This site has no analytics, advertising, accounts or forms. Here's what does happen when you visit.">
    <article class="page-head wrap privacy">
        <p class="mono muted" data-reveal>Updated 4 November 2026</p>
        <h1 class="display privacy__title" data-split>Privacy<span class="stop" aria-hidden="true"></span></h1>
        <p class="lead privacy__lead" data-reveal>This site doesn't track you. It has no analytics, advertising, accounts or forms.</p>

        <div class="privacy__text prose">
            <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
            <p>Rafaela Henriques, Kortrijk, Belgium. You can reach me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="link">{site.email}</a>.</p>

            <h2>If you email me</h2>
            <p>I receive your address and whatever you write, and I use them only to reply. My email runs on Gmail, so Google also processes those messages.</p>

            <h2>Hosting</h2>
            <p>
                Cloudflare serves this site. Like any web host, it handles technical data such as your IP address to deliver the pages and protect the site from abuse. See
                <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's privacy policy ↗</a>.
                The fonts are served from this site too, so nothing goes to a font service.
            </p>

            <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
            <p>This site sets no cookies. It keeps up to three small notes in your own browser, and none of them is sent anywhere:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><code>theme</code>: your light or dark choice, kept only if you use the switch, until you clear it.</li>
                <li><code>loader-seen</code>: so the loading screen plays once per visit. It goes when you close the tab.</li>
                <li><code>wipe</code>: starts the transition between pages. It goes when you close the tab.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Videos on Vimeo</h2>
            <p>
                The Wolf & Sheep and Miles & Meals pages each have a walkthrough hosted on Vimeo. Nothing loads from Vimeo until you press play. Once you do, Vimeo receives your IP address and may set cookies, as described in
                <a href="https://vimeo.com/privacy" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vimeo's privacy policy ↗</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
            <p>Links to places like GitHub, LinkedIn, Figma and my live projects lead to sites with their own privacy policies.</p>

            <h2>Your rights</h2>
            <p>
                Under the GDPR you can ask me what data I hold about you, and have it corrected or deleted, by emailing me. You can also complain to the
                <a href="https://www.dataprotectionauthority.be/citizen" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Belgian Data Protection Authority ↗</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</Base>

<style>
    .privacy {
        padding-bottom: var(--section);
    }

    .privacy__lead {
        max-width: 24ch;
        margin-top: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
    }

    .privacy__text {
        max-width: 62ch;
        margin-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px);
    }
</style>
